 "id": "inference-engineering",
 "group": "Systems and GPU Programming",
 "title": "Inference Engineering Drills",
 "blurb": "Build the pieces of an LLM serving engine in code: attention variants that shrink the KV cache, tiled attention, sampling and MoE routing, a paged and prefix-shared cache, speculative decoding, low-bit weight formats, and the schedulers, metrics and capacity models that decide what a deployment costs.",
 "prereq": "Comfortable with PyTorch tensor code and with how causal attention in a Transformer works; knowing what a KV cache stores is a good starting point.",
